{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.TorusKnotShellBinding","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.TorusKnotShellBinding","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.first_shell_gap_large","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.first_shell_gap_large","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-knot-shell-binding.lean#L170-L171","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.first_shell_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.first_shell_gap","kind":"def","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-knot-shell-binding.lean#L165-L168","doc":"First shell gap: He-4 → Li-5 gives ratio ≈ 14.8.\nThis uses the witness data from sequential-nucleus-builder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.eigenvalue_ratio_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.eigenvalue_ratio_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-knot-shell-binding.lean#L156-L163","doc":"The eigenvalue ratio grows with shell size. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.shell_eigenvalue_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shell_eigenvalue_ratio","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-knot-shell-binding.lean#L146-L154","doc":"The dominant eigenvalue of the torus knot transfer matrix\nT(c_n, d_n) at the inter-shell boundary.  For T_{2,n_s},\nthis scales as q^{n_s}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.magic_from_shells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.magic_from_shells","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-knot-shell-binding.lean#L132-L136","doc":"Verification: cumulative sums of shell_sizes equal magic_numbers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.magic_numbers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.magic_numbers","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-knot-shell-binding.lean#L129-L130","doc":"The magic numbers are cumulative sums of shell sizes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.shell_sizes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shell_sizes","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-knot-shell-binding.lean#L126-L127","doc":"Shell sizes from the torus knot hierarchy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.inter_shell_preserves_normal_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.inter_shell_preserves_normal_form","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-knot-shell-binding.lean#L98-L116","doc":"Inter-shell step preserves normal form.\nWhen a shell of size n_s closes and the next nucleon crosses via\nthe Chebyshev element (c_{n_s} σ + d_{n_s}), the Gröbner division\nalgorithm produces a normal form — by the same main theorem used\nfor intra-shell steps.\n\nThis is structurally identical to hopf_link_preserves_normal_form\nin shell-closure-normal-form.lean: the crossing element is linear\nin σ (no squares), so the product N̄_A · (c σ + d) may introduce\nσ² terms that the Hecke relation resolves, and the division\nalgorithm terminates with a unique normal form remainder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.chebyshev_crossing_coefficients","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.chebyshev_crossing_coefficients","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-knot-shell-binding.lean#L75-L83","doc":"The Chebyshev crossing data for T_{2,n} decomposes as (c_n, d_n).\nThe key observation is that the crossing element c_n σ + d_n is\nlinear in σ (degree 1 in the Hecke generator), so it introduces\nno σ² terms by itself — only products with existing normal form\nwords can create squares, which the Gröbner division resolves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.chebyshev_crossing_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.chebyshev_crossing_one","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-knot-shell-binding.lean#L71-L73","doc":"Base case: c₁ = 1, d₁ = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.chebyshev_crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.chebyshev_crossing","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-knot-shell-binding.lean#L61-L69","doc":"Chebyshev crossing coefficients for T_{2,n}.\nReturns (c_n, d_n) where T(c_n, d_n) is the inter-shell\ntransfer matrix for a shell of size n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.division_terminates_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.division_terminates_unique","kind":"axiom","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-knot-shell-binding.lean#L42-L49","doc":"Forward declaration — the Gröbner division algorithm terminates and\nproduces a unique normal form remainder.  Justified by\n[unital-groebner-bases:thm:ugb-main-theorem]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsNormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsNormalForm","kind":"axiom","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-knot-shell-binding.lean#L37-L40","doc":"Forward declaration — see shell-closure-normal-form.lean for the\nfull structure definition with no_squares, no_far_comm, no_yang_baxter. ","signatureChunk":0}]}